  "description": "The easiest way to send email over SMTP from .NET, built on MailKit: a fluent message builder with HTML and text bodies, attachments, CC/BCC and Reply-To, TLS by default, OAuth2, batch sending over one connection, and one-line dependency injection setup.",
  "id": "Fayakun.Email",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-09T12:51:10.69Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "TY6h+mPImpVg0ZyqPfci4tBpZj/1bys9Wef3P7Q8tRYRiiDQ78aMjKC+bB2Qw0vVlbkhRqYARMwKVw4PVTckpg==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 94530,
  "published": "2026-11-09T12:44:21.67Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0 (breaking)\n- Rebuilt on MailKit, Microsoft's recommended replacement for System.Net.Mail.SmtpClient.\n- New API: EmailMessage (fluent builder), IEmailSender (from EmailSenderFactory.Create or services.AddEmailSender) and SmtpOptions. Replaces Email and SmtpConfig.\n- Send results report success, the server response and the message ID, or the failure instead of throwing.\n- New: HTML and plain-text bodies together, attachments, Reply-To, custom headers and priority (sets the Priority, X-Priority and Importance headers, so Outlook, Gmail and Apple Mail all see it).\n- New: SendManyAsync sends many messages over one connection.\n- New: OAuth2 (XOAUTH2) authentication, CancellationToken support and a configurable timeout.\n- New: services.AddEmailSender(options => ...) for dependency injection.\n- Secure by default: TLS is required (STARTTLS, or implicit TLS on port 465).\n- Fix: messages are no longer sent with a placeholder subject or body when none is set.\n- Fix: credentials no longer override UseDefaultCredentials. NTLM default credentials are not supported in 2.0.\n- Targets netstandard2.0, netstandard2.1, net462, net8.0 and net10.0 (net40 and net45 dropped).",
